# Prediction engine.
#
# predict.db is derived and rebuildable -- always ignored.
#
# data/odds/*.jsonl.gz is the IRREPLACEABLE half: raw venue payloads that cannot
# be re-fetched once a market moves or closes. It is NOT committed, and that is a
# deliberate correction to the original design, which asserted it was.
#
# The arithmetic: ~3 MB gzipped per nightly run is ~90 MB/month and ~1 GB/year of
# incompressible blobs in git. A retention rule nobody can sustain is worse than an
# honest local-only one -- the first time it hurt, someone would delete the history
# wholesale, which is precisely the loss the rule existed to prevent.
#
# PHASE 2 MUST DECIDE a durable backup that is not git (object storage, or a
# retention window that prunes raw payloads past N days and keeps the normalised
# odds series, which is small). Until then this data lives on one disk and that is
# a known, recorded risk -- not an oversight.
data/predict.db
data/predict.db-journal
data/predict.db-wal
